      <div class="cs-split">
        <div class="cs-col">
          <h3 class="cs-finding">Validation plan</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-col cs-prose cs-prose--loose">
          <p>Binu is pre-launch, so there are no usage metrics yet. The next step is a comprehension test with 5 people on the live demo.<br /><br />If people confuse evidence grades with safety ratings, that's the signal to rework how grades are labeled before adding any new features. After launch, analytics will track whether people open the explanations and research, not just the grade.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-stack">
        <span class="cs-lead-label">The test checks whether people can:</span>
        <div class="cs-grid cs-grid--tight">
          <Card size="sm" gap={28}>
            <span class="cs-check-num">1</span>
            <p class="cs-check-text">Explain what an evidence grade means in their own words</p>
          </Card>
          <Card size="sm" gap={28}>
            <span class="cs-check-num">2</span>
            <p class="cs-check-text">Tell evidence quality apart from ingredient safety</p>
          </Card>
          <Card size="sm" gap={28}>
            <span class="cs-check-num">3</span>
            <p class="cs-check-text">Compare 2 products and say which claims are better supported</p>
          </Card>
          <Card size="sm" gap={28}>
            <span class="cs-check-num">4</span>
            <p class="cs-check-text">Get value from the explanation without feeling overwhelmed</p>
          </Card>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- LEARNINGS -->
    <section class="cs-stack cs-gap-40 cs-section">
      <SectionLabel>Learnings</SectionLabel>
      <div class="cs-row">
        <Card basis={300}>
          <h3 class="cs-learning-title">Research earlier</h3>
          <p class="cs-learning-body">Even 2 early conversations changed the roadmap. Testing assumptions sooner would have caught things like the skincare diary before we scoped them.</p>
        </Card>
        <Card basis={300}>
          <h3 class="cs-learning-title">Trust lives in the system and the interface</h3>
          <p class="cs-learning-body">Trust affected the grading logic, the content language, the information hierarchy and how visible the sources are.</p>
        </Card>
        <Card basis={300}>
          <h3 class="cs-learning-title">Product restraint is a design decision</h3>
          <p class="cs-learning-body">The most valuable choice was not building the expected parity features before the evidence-first value was clear.</p>
        </Card>
      </div>
    </section>

